@page "/components/load-on-scroll"
@model HTMX.Application.Web.Pages.Components.LoadOnScrollModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Load on scroll";
    ViewData["Section"] = "Components";
}
<header page-header>
    <nav breadcrumbs aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol><li><a asp-page="/Index">Home</a></li><li><a asp-page="./Index">Components</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Load on scroll</span></li></ol>
    </nav>
    <div page-header="title-row">
        <h1 tabindex="-1" autofocus="@Model.HeadingFocused">Load on scroll</h1>
    </div>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
        The active organizations by name, ten at a time, the next ten added as the last row comes into view, up to a
        hundred. Load more, above the list, adds them as well.
    </p>
</header>

@*
    The list grows as its last row comes into view, so anything under it would move further away with each load, and
    could not be reached until the list stopped growing. So nothing follows it: the pager, which the brand puts at the
    bottom of a list's card, sits above the table here, and the card ends with the list.

    The status line stays on the page, empty, and each load the user did not ask for writes into it what came, which a
    screen reader says, since such a load moves no keyboard. The rows, the pager and the status line are each drawn by
    the page and by the answer to a load (_LoadOnScrollAnswer) alike.
*@
<section card aria-labelledby="more-heading">
    <header card="header"><h2 id="more-heading">Organizations</h2></header>
    <partial name="_LoadOnScrollPager" model="Model" />
    <p class="sr-only" role="status" id="more-status"></p>
    <div grid="scroll">
        <table grid>
            <caption class="sr-only">Active organizations, by name</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Name</th>
                    <th scope="col">Industry</th>
                    <th scope="col">Contacts</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="more-rows">
                <partial name="_LoadMoreRows" model="Model" />
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>
